text:
10.

I met a Lady once at Stratford fair;
She was the loveliest thing I ever saw;
But when she told me of her love for me
She died, and never wrote to me again!

So you’re young--I was once as young
As you are now--though younger by far;
And there was joy in every smile I gave
To lips that still were tender to me now;

Yet with a memory so quick I knew
That each was passing of its youth away;
Each smile like a bird flying on high
Had wings too weak for flight for long to stay.

For Time does more than years advance;
Though one is old he is not always wise;
He carries change within his hand,
Which changes what we used to prize.
